00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.810
I wish I could give you a hickey
on the inside, too.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:02.190
You can't! Right?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.150
Still, I wanted to say it.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.980
I want all of the places that I can reach.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.860
Do you want me, too, Takato?

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.740
<i>This kind of thing embarrasses me.</i>

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.280
...you. Want... you...

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.080
I want you... Chunta.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.080
<i>I'm embarrassed of myself,
wanting to be honest.</i>

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.040
<i>I'm embarrassed, but I can't hide anything.</i>

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:29.920
<i>I like him so much that my head
can't keep up with my emotions.</i>

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.550
What time is it?

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.010
Hey. Are you asleep?

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.270
<i>He's right here.</i>

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.020
Chunta.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.940
Do you want to live together?

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:46.770
Nah, no way.

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:48.730
What am I saying?

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:49.940
Do you mean it?

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.530
You... You were awake?

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:55.610
You were only pretending to be asleep?

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.530
I woke up because you called my name.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:01.330
More importantly, Takato,
were you serious about what you said?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.540
No, that was, um...

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.880
Stupid. I didn't say... uh...

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.340
I'm so happy right now.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.970
<i>Are you an idiot?
What's there to be so happy about?</i>

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:17.510
Fine, whatever. Yeah, all right.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.470
I'll search for an apartment!

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.770
What kind of place would you like?

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.310
- I'll leave it to you.
- Okay.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:27.980
Oh, Takato. Would you tell me
that you like me once more?

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.940
I don't come cheap.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:30.690
A thousand yen—

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:31.530
Go to hell.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:34.490
<i>I'm an idiot, too.</i>

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:38.570
Sheesh. For once, try to keep it turned down.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.040
- It?
- That needlessly bright aura!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.200
You're blinding me!

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.210
That was Chihiro Ayagi and Takato Saijo,

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.710
from the stage production of "The Red Leaf Ogre,"
which opens next month.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.760
Can I have a word?

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:57.890
I heard everything.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:01.140
How dare you mock me like that? Hey!

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.520
Oh, I have no idea what you're referring to.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.230
- Ow!
- Jeez! Always screwing around!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.610
Huh? You're not mad?

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:12.480
Are your eyes just for decoration?
Yes, I'm mad!

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:16.400
Well, I share some of the blame
that night for getting drunk.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:18.570
And you were just being mischievous, right?

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.120
Just mischievous?

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:24.540
The way I hear it,
you're all alone without any friends,

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.910
and you always get dumped by girlfriends,

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.630
so you were so lonely
that you thought you'd pick on me.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.340
That's what Chun... what he told me.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:37.550
You seem like a shrewd guy, but
apparently you're pathetic in several respects.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.510
Path... Wait a second!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:43.470
I'm pretty serious about you, Mr. Saijo.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.930
Ayagi.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.230
Okay, okay.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.810
You can drop it.

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:56.490
Look, if you really want to challenge me,
do it onstage, and I'll be happy to take you on.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:00.870
But if you come at me half-seriously,
I'll steal the whole show and leave you nothing.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:04.700
So try not to embarrass yourself
out there, junior.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.080
Mr. Saijo, I seriously will—

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.960
Oh, there he is!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.670
Mr. Saijo!

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.290
Narumiya!

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:16.710
I heard your location shoot
finished early the other day.

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:20.010
That's right! It was awesome!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.680
Galaxy Agency
Ryo Narumiya

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:24.010
Everyone was influenced by Junta's spirit
on the last day!

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.520
We finished that day without any mistakes!

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:31.190
The typhoon left that morning, too, leading
some of us to think it was the angel's power.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.980
He really is an angel!

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.110
Huh.

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.190
Oh, yeah! You're Mr. Ayagi, aren't you?

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:38.570
Huh? Yeah.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:43.280
I've been holding on to something
from Junta to give to you.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.780
- To me?
- Yes.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.750
The angel of ice floe, Clione!

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.870
If you squeeze this part, it makes a noise.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:53.540
<i>By the way, Chihiro Ayagi,</i>

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:57.340
<i>I've heard rumors that you pillow-talked
your way up the ladder. Is that true?</i>

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:03.140
<i>Go right ahead. The women I've bedded...</i>

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.140
Pillow?

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:04.220
Give me that!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:05.680
What is that?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.520
Was that Ch... Azumaya talking to you?

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.810
I think it's just your imagination!

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:15.310
It was you! Let's hear it!
What's this about pillows?

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.400
Hey, brat! Knock it off!

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:18.570
Mr. Saijo.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.740
Damn it! Please excuse me for today!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:25.740
Mr. Ayagi!
What was that bit about "pillows"?

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:28.160
Shut up! Don't follow me!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.500
What was that about?

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.500
Yes?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.670
<i>Good work today, Takato!</i>

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.920
<i>Has the intruder left by now?</i>

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.420
Where are you spying me from?

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:42.220
<i>Where? I'm about to leave the studio.</i>

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.840
Liar! Where are you?!

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:44.970
Here?!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:49.770
<i>Oh, come on! I wouldn't hide in a garbage can!</i>

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.020
Hey! Then where are you? I'm scared!

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.650
I'm scared! Mr. Sasaki!

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:59.980
Publisher

00:20:57.980 --> 00:20:59.980
Very nice!

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.320
Hase, you really do good work!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.990
Weekly Fuyufumi
Editor-in-Chief
Koki Tanabe

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:06.200
I wish you would consider
going exclusive with us.

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.290
Why don't we get sushi together next time?

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:10.540
No need.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.870
You don't have to suck up to me
for boring work like this.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.540
Independent Cameraman
Jiro Hasegawa

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.750
Oh, no enthusiasm!

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:19.460
Well, recently
nothing splashy has been happening.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:24.050
Then how about taking a gamble and
staking out a place where there is no smoke?

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.010
A gamble?

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:28.890
Yeah. It's about time we got a big scoop.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.720
Let's see.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:36.230
If you land me some gossip around this,

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:40.610
info about women, money, and so on,
I'll pay through the nose!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:44.530
Vulgar. A wholesome subject like this.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:48.030
We're in a vulgar business, aren't we, Hase?

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:54.330
Well, I'll think about it.

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:30.720
Mr. Saijo. I really like you.

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:34.310
I'm sorry. Even if you hate me...

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:39.140
hug7
"Can I keep liking you?"
